A single T8 upgraded island will bring in an easy 1mil silver/day by processing journals off the market, at market price. This million arrives at the cost of time of journal distribution, as risk has been eliminated from the equation.

Prices in Albion have inflated. Resources, armor drops, weapon drops, relics, hell- even pups are ridiculously priced now. So yea, of course they raised the price of the islands. Inflation, inflation, inflation. Sure, prices have inflated, but it's much better to add silver sinks players want to use, rather than ones they feel they have to use. It's also better to hit wealthy players with the sinks, as opposed to new players. ... Sure, prices have inflated, but it's much better to add silver sinks players want to use, rather than ones they feel they have to use. It's also better to hit wealthy players with the sinks, as opposed to new players. These silver sinks do affect the wealthy, and more veteran players. Way more than it impacts new players.. - higher tier gear, high repair price (new player aint wearing t8.1 to fame farms) - Higher conversion of silver to fame credits (new players won't have a 100 spec build that they're grinding fame farms, hg's or cGvG with) Honestly, most of 

So don't upgrade it to 6/6? You are paying a premium for having a single location that features an additional farm plot/house plot. For some this extra slot is valuable, as time is money. For others (most) it's not. Islands contain zero ZERO zero risk. Why wouldn't you want to go this route? Because it is expensive as hell to start. The cost to go 6/6/ island is like 14m. Ok, now populate all those slots with buildings. What tier? Tier 8? Let's go with 40m total material cost. Now what? FURNITURE. That ain't cheap. Add another 40m. Wanna raise animals? Rare mounts aint cheap! 500k a pup adds up quick. So let's just round up now to 100mil to build a T8 6/6/ ready island. What does that do for me? A single T8 upgraded island will bring in an easy 1mil silver/day by processing journals off the market, at market price. This million arrives at the cost of time of journal distribution, as risk has been eliminated from the equation.

@OP, I'd ignore the forum bullies (who no doubt upgraded their islands under the old system). What I see in what you're saying is that an island is quite possibly the first huge price tag a new player will see, yet there's no corresponding information given as to why they're so valuable, so the price seems arbitrary and imbalanced. The farm plots are worth it, however. For example, each plot gives me about 80 carrots or so on average, which I can sell for 300+ silver each per day. That's 80 x 300 = 24K per plot x 5 plots = 120K per day on a maxed island, which is roughly 3.6 million silver a month. (That doesn't count what you can do with houses and labourers, although I wouldn't bother with most crafting stations.) So, at 3.6m per month, you can make back that 14m in four months just farming, and then it's pure profit for the rest of your time in Albion.

@OP, I'd ignore the forum bullies (who no doubt upgraded their islands under the old system). If by old system you refer to after April 2019 when I recreated a character, coming back to albion after having played in beta 1, sure. Still, given that I also purchased and upgraded a guild island all by myself, expect me to still call bullshit on that whine. If I had 14M, I would have been able to buy 10 sets of T8 equipment （although they are normal）and they would have created more profits and happiness for me than islands! 10 sets of T8 equipment that have roughly the Item Power of T4.3 E/MP, with no mastery... a short lived happiness if you want my insight, and doubtful profitability... Nonetheless, please, explain how "14M silver= have played 99% of the game", I'm interested. Really. The post was edited 3 times, last by Inkless (Oct 24th 2019, 11:53am).
